{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאמר ה' אל משה", :translit "vayomer Hashem el Moshe", :gloss "and YHWH said to Moses"} {:he "והלא כבר נא' וידבר", :translit "vehalo kvar na' vaydaber", :gloss "but was it not already stated 'and He spoke'"} {:he "אלא הדיבור הא' לו' לו מעשה פרה", :translit "elah ha-dibur ha-rishon lo, lo ma'aseh parah", :gloss "rather the first utterance to him, to him: the rite of the cow"} {:he "שגם היא צריכה פרישה ז' ימים קודם", :translit "shegam hi tzrikhah hafrashah shiv'ah yamim kodem", :gloss "which also requires separation seven days beforehand"} {:he "אחרי מות שני", :translit "acharei mot shnei", :gloss "after the death of two"} {:he "פרה אדומה", :translit "parah adumah", :gloss "red cow"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "אחרי מות שני", :spells "פרה"} {:kind :gematria, :a "אחרי מות שני", :b "פרה אדומה"}], :frame {:text "The priest who burns the red heifer must separate himself for seven days prior, a requirement the Tannaitic source compares to the High Priest's seclusion before Yom Kippur: just as the one who burns the red heifer separates for seven days, so the High Priest who performs the Yom Kippur service separates for seven days (Yoma 2a, Parah 3:1). Ba'al HaTurim reads the doubling 'to him, to him' as a verbal link between these two rites of separation.", :sources ["Yoma 2a" "Mishnah Parah 3:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "אחרי מות שני", :spells "פרה", :letters ["א" "מ" "ש"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :gematria, :a "אחרי מות שני", :a-value 1025, :b "פרה אדומה", :b-value 341, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:40.086104908Z", :model "glm-5.2"}